      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION: 4 CORE ARCHITECTURAL PILLARS (DEEP DIVE MATRIX) -->
    <section class="section" aria-label="Core Engineering Pillars">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-meta reveal-item">
          <span class="section-index">// 02.1</span>
          <span class="section-tag">CORE ARCHITECTURAL MATRIX</span>
        </div>

        <div class="skills-grid grid-4">
          <!-- Pillar 1: HTML5 -->
          <article class="skill-card reveal-item" data-tilt>
            <div class="skill-card-inner">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <span class="skill-index">01</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">DOM_ARCHITECTURE</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="skill-title">HTML5 Semantic Systems</h2>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Engineering accessible, search-optimized, and clean document flow. Structuring DOM trees that assistive technologies navigate effortlessly and browsers render with optimal compositing.
              </p>
              <div style="margin: 16px 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8;">
                <div>&bull; Semantic Landmark Elements (&lt;header&gt;, &lt;main&gt;, &lt;article&gt;)</div>
                <div>&bull; WCAG 2.1 AA Screen-Reader Compliance</div>
                <div>&bull; Social OpenGraph &amp; Metadata Standards</div>
                <div>&bull; Preconnect &amp; Asset Optimization Hints</div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-code-preview" aria-hidden="true">
                <code>&lt;main role="main" aria-label="core"&gt;</code>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Pillar 2: CSS3 -->
          <article class="skill-card reveal-item" data-tilt>
            <div class="skill-card-inner">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <span class="skill-index">02</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">SPATIAL_STYLING</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="skill-title">CSS3 &amp; Design Tokens</h2>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Building fluid, mathematical layout systems without heavy CSS frameworks. Leveraging CSS Custom Properties, asymmetric 12-column Grid, fluid clamp() formulas, and GPU-composited animations.
              </p>
              <div style="margin: 16px 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8;">
                <div>&bull; Fluid Typography (clamp() equations)</div>
                <div>&bull; Asymmetric CSS Grid &amp; Flexbox Layouts</div>
                <div>&bull; Hardware-Accelerated 3D Transform Matrices</div>
                <div>&bull; Curated Glassmorphism &amp; Backdrop Filters</div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-code-preview" aria-hidden="true">
                <code>clamp(2.5rem, 5vw + 1rem, 6rem);</code>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Pillar 3: JavaScript -->
          <article class="skill-card reveal-item" data-tilt>
            <div class="skill-card-inner">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <span class="skill-index">03</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">ENGINE_LOGIC</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="skill-title">JavaScript (ES6+)</h2>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Client-side execution logic, asynchronous pipelines, event loop comprehension, DOM reactivity, and hardware-accelerated canvas animation loops with zero framework lock-in.
              </p>
              <div style="margin: 16px 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8;">
                <div>&bull; Asynchronous Pipelines &amp; Promise Chains</div>
                <div>&bull; Event-Driven Architecture &amp; IntersectionObservers</div>
                <div>&bull; Canvas 2D &amp; Three.js WebGL Integration</div>
                <div>&bull; Linear Interpolation (Lerp) Physics</div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-code-preview" aria-hidden="true">
                <code>requestAnimationFrame(renderLoop);</code>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Pillar 4: C Programming -->
          <article class="skill-card reveal-item" data-tilt>
            <div class="skill-card-inner">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <span class="skill-index">04</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">SYSTEMS_CORE</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="skill-title">C Programming</h2>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                The scholastic anchor of my engineering discipline. Understanding physical RAM, dynamic memory allocation (malloc/free), pointer arithmetic, structs, and fundamental data structures.
              </p>
              <div style="margin: 16px 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8;">
                <div>&bull; Dynamic Heap Allocations &amp; Memory Safety</div>
                <div>&bull; Pointer Arithmetic &amp; Struct Modeling</div>
                <div>&bull; Data Structures (Linked Lists, Stacks, Queues)</div>
                <div>&bull; Algorithmic Efficiency &amp; Big-O Reasoning</div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-code-preview" aria-hidden="true">
                <code>int *mem = malloc(sizeof(int) * 64);</code>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION: THE DUALITY PHILOSOPHY -->
    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;" aria-label="Engineering Philosophy">
      <div class="container">
        <div style="background: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.75); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 44px); border-radius: 20px; backdrop-filter: blur(16px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);" class="reveal-item" data-tilt>
          <div class="section-meta">
            <span class="section-index">// 02.2</span>
            <span class="section-tag">ENGINEERING PRINCIPLE: THE LOW-TO-HIGH DUALITY</span>
          </div>

          <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-luxury); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.2vw, 2.8rem); color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 20px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">
            How Low-Level Systems Thinking Transforms Web Development
          </h2>

          <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 24px; margin-top: 24px;">
            <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); padding: 24px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);">
              <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: #FFFFFF; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 600;">[CONCEPT: MEMORY AWARENESS]</div>
              <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65;">
                In C, unmanaged memory causes immediate crashes or leaks. In JavaScript, understanding garbage collection prevents hidden memory retention in detached DOM nodes and animation loops.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); padding: 24px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);">
              <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: #FFFFFF; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 600;">[CONCEPT: TIME COMPLEXITY]</div>
              <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65;">
                Writing sorting algorithms in C clarifies why unoptimized iterations freeze the browser thread. Every DOM query and array transformation is evaluated for computational cost.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); padding: 24px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);">
              <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: #FFFFFF; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 600;">[CONCEPT: ARCHITECTURAL DISCIPLINE]</div>
              <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65;">
                C demands strict compilation and zero implicit magic. This translates into disciplined, modular vanilla JavaScript with explicit variable scopes and predictable state flow.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION: GROWTH VECTOR / ROADMAP -->
    <section class="section trajectory-section" aria-label="Learning Trajectory">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-meta reveal-item">
          <span class="section-index">// 02.3</span>
