          <p style="font-size: 15.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 640px; line-height: 1.65;">
            An honest, forward-looking roadmap of the technologies and engineering disciplines I am actively expanding into.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 24px;">
          <!-- Vector 1 -->
          <div style="background: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.75); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); padding: 32px; border-radius: 18px; backdrop-filter: blur(16px);" class="reveal-item" data-tilt>
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 16px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px;">
              <span style="color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: 600;">VECTOR 01</span>
              <span style="color: #FFFFFF; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1); padding: 3px 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); border-radius: 4px;">ACTIVE FOCUS</span>
            </div>
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-luxury); font-size: 22px; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">JavaScript Internals &amp; Advanced C</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 16px;">
              Deepening understanding of the V8 execution model, microtask queues, and event loops alongside linked lists, stacks, and binary trees in C.
            </p>
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8;">
              <div>&bull; Event loop concurrency &amp; Web Workers</div>
              <div>&bull; Dynamic memory management &amp; file I/O in C</div>
              <div>&bull; Modular ES6+ bundling principles</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Vector 2 -->
          <div style="background: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.75); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); padding: 32px; border-radius: 18px; backdrop-filter: blur(16px);" class="reveal-item" data-tilt>
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 16px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px;">
              <span style="color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: 600;">VECTOR 02</span>
              <span style="color: var(--text-muted); background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05); padding: 3px 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15); border-radius: 4px;">NEXT HORIZON</span>
            </div>
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-luxury); font-size: 22px; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">Custom GLSL Shaders &amp; Modern Tooling</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 16px;">
              Progressing from basic Three.js into custom vertex/fragment shaders written in GLSL, paired with modern build pipelines and TypeScript.
            </p>
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8;">
              <div>&bull; GLSL math: vector transformations &amp; noise</div>
              <div>&bull; Component architecture &amp; TypeScript basics</div>
              <div>&bull; Web Accessibility (WCAG AAA standards)</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Vector 3 -->
          <div style="background: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.75); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); padding: 32px; border-radius: 18px; backdrop-filter: blur(16px);" class="reveal-item" data-tilt>
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 16px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px;">
              <span style="color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: 600;">VECTOR 03</span>
              <span style="color: var(--text-muted); background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05); padding: 3px 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15); border-radius: 4px;">VISION</span>
            </div>
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-luxury); font-size: 22px; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600;">High-Craft Creative Development</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 16px;">
              Evolving into a versatile creative developer capable of conceptualizing and engineering digital experiences celebrated for aesthetic and technical excellence.
            </p>
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8;">
              <div>&bull; Interactive 3D spatial web design</div>
              <div>&bull; High-performance computational layouts</div>
              <div>&bull; Zero-framework creative engineering</div>
